      "intrinsic": "Symbol.dispose / Symbol.asyncDispose",
      "sourceStatus": "Genuine well-known engine symbols present behind explicit-resource compile macro; main recipe enables it.",
      "nodeRequirement": "Node generic Symbol property copying derives primordial SymbolDispose/SymbolAsyncDispose aliases from actual Symbol properties. These are not direct pure-primordials assertions, but unchanged consumers such as stream constructors attach methods with SymbolAsyncDispose; absent symbols would produce incorrect public methods.",
      "engineEvidence": "js/public/Symbol.h includes both well-known codes under IF_EXPLICIT_RESOURCE_MANAGEMENT. TypeDecls.h implements that macro using ENABLE_EXPLICIT_RESOURCE_MANAGEMENT. SymbolClassFinish installs every engine well-known symbol as readonly/permanent Symbol constructor property. Runtime explicit-resource pref controls parser/DisposableStack selection; this symbol installation loop itself has no runtime-pref gate.",
